# Walkthrough - Timetable Event Fix

I have resolved the issue where personal events in the timetable were not displaying or functioning correctly.

## Changes Made

### Frontend
- **Updated [page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/timetable/page.tsx)**:
    - Added logic to the horizontal view to correctly identify and render personal events.
    - Fixed the rendering of event titles (previously showing as "CLS").
    - Implemented a category-based label (e.g., "STUDY", "MEETING", "PERSONAL") for events.
    - Added a delete button to the horizontal view for personal events, matching the vertical view's functionality.
    - Improved consistency of event styling (dashed borders and color-coded labels).

## Verification Results

### Automated Browser Testing
I used a browser subagent to verify the fix in the actual application:
1. **Event Creation**: A new event "Verify Fix Horizontal" was successfully created in Horizontal mode.
2. **Title & Label Verification**: The event block correctly displayed the title and the "PERSONAL" category label instead of the generic "CLS" label.
3. **Deletion**: The delete button was visible and functional, successfully removing the event from the timetable.

![Verification Recording](file:///Users/oli/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f51e80ec-111f-4075-afdb-481a07df1785/verify_timetable_fix_horizontal_1772385841030.webp)

## Final Status
The timetable now correctly handles both academic classes and personal events in all view modes.
